{"name":"Blue Java Banana","hex":"#c1ebff","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"java","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blend of coffee imported from the island of Java.","Coffee in general."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dance popular in France in the early 20th century."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/java"},{"term":"banana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The elongated curved tropical fruit of a banana plant, which grows in bunches and has a creamy flesh and a smooth skin. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","In particular, the sweet, yellow fruit of the Cavendish banana cultivar, which may be eaten raw, as distinct from e.g. a plantain for cooking."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Curved like a banana, especially of a ball in flight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Java banana","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Java is a hardy, cold-tolerant banana cultivar known for its sweet aromatic fruit, which is said to have an ice cream-like consistency and flavor reminiscent of vanilla. It is native to Southeast Asia and is a hybrid of two species of banana native to Southeast Asia—Musa balbisiana and Musa acuminata."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Starr-091112-1064-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824362538683%29.jpg/330px-Starr-091112-1064-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824362538683%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Java_banana","wikidata":"Q4929278"},{"title":"Java","blocks":[{"text":"Java is one of the Greater Sunda Islands in the South East Asian country of Indonesia. It is bordered by the Indian Ocean to the south and the Java Sea to the north. Java is the world's most populous island, home to an estimated 159.2 million people; about 56% of the Indonesian population, while constituting only 7% of the country's land area. Indonesia's capital city, Jakarta, is located on Java's northwestern coast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Java_Topography.png/330px-Java_Topography.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java","wikidata":"Q3757"},{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Ice_Cream_Banana_%28Blue_Java%29.jpg/500px-Ice_Cream_Banana_%28Blue_Java%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Ice_Cream_Banana_%28Blue_Java%29.jpg/500px-Ice_Cream_Banana_%28Blue_Java%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bunch of Blue Java bananas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIce_Cream_Banana_(Blue_Java).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Starr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824895836571%29.jpg/500px-Starr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824895836571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Starr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824895836571%29.jpg/1280px-Starr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824895836571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Starr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824895836571%29.jpg/500px-Starr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_%2824895836571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue Java tree in Maui, Hawaii","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStarr-091112-9540-Musa_x_paradisiaca-Iholena_habit-West_Maui-Maui_(24895836571).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg/500px-Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg/1280px-Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg/500px-Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Bromo in Malang, East Java","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg/500px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg/500px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parahyangan highland near Buitenzorg (now Bogor, West Java), c. 1865–1872","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.